# Xero MCP server configuration. Pick ONE authentication mode.
#
# Set only the variables for the mode you are using. In particular, a public
# (PKCE) app has no client secret: leaving a placeholder in XERO_CLIENT_SECRET
# makes the server authenticate as a confidential app and every token request
# fails.

# ── Mode 1: Custom Connections ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A machine-to-machine connection to one organisation.
# XERO_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
# XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here

# ── Mode 2: Bearer token ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A token obtained elsewhere. Lasts 30 minutes and is not renewed.
# XERO_CLIENT_BEARER_TOKEN=your_bearer_token

# ── Mode 3: Refresh token (recommended for interactive apps) ──────────────────
# Path to the token file written by `npm run auth`. The server renews the
# access token from it, so this mode survives longer than 30 minutes.
# XERO_TOKEN_FILE=/absolute/path/to/.xero-tokens.json
#
# The client id is read from the token file. Set it here only to override, or
# for a first-time bootstrap with no token file yet.
# XERO_CLIENT_ID=your_client_id_here
#
# Only for a CONFIDENTIAL app. Leave unset for a public PKCE app — a non-empty
# value switches the server to basic auth and refreshes will be rejected.
# XERO_CLIENT_SECRET=your_client_secret_here

# ── Optional, any mode ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pin the server to one organisation, by name or tenant id.
# XERO_TENANT_ID=Your Organisation Name
# Override the scopes requested at authorisation.
# XERO_SCOPES=openid profile email offline_access accounting.settings
